<ResourceDictionary xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui" xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">
    <!-- Phone button icons — the TabIcons/LibraryIcons family on the same 24x24 grid.
         Outline glyphs = 1.8u stroke (round caps/joins) expanded to fill; single-stroke glyphs
         (chevrons, ✕, check) 2.0u; transport (play, pause, forward, rewind) solid with softly
         rounded corners, all four 15u tall. Shapes that repeat a meaning are the same geometry as
         the matched set (shuffle, repeat, list, dots, heart, search).
         Every string starts with "M0 0ZM24 24Z": two zero-area contours at the grid corners.
         PathIcon draws Data with Stretch=Uniform, so without them each glyph would be stretched to
         its own bounds (stroke weight changing from glyph to glyph, the play triangle's optical
         shift undone). With them, a PathIcon's Width/Height is the 24-grid box: at 24 a glyph is
         drawn 1:1 and the stroke is 1.8 dp. Typical boxes: 24 icon buttons and sheet rows,
         20 inside pills, 30 mini player transport, 36 queue pill transport, 44/54 Now Playing.
         Holes wind opposite to their parents, so EvenOdd (default) and NonZero render the same. -->
    <!-- play: solid triangle with lightly softened tips at Apple's play.fill proportions (Play pill, mini player, queue pill, Now Playing) -->
    <StreamGeometry x:Key="PhPlayFill">M0 0ZM24 24ZM7.9 5.14L18.57 10.99Q20.4 12 18.57 13.01L7.9 18.86Q6.2 19.8 6.2 17.86L6.2 6.14Q6.2 4.2 7.9 5.14Z</StreamGeometry>
    <!-- pause: two solid bars, about a quarter of their height wide with a narrow gap, like Apple's pause.fill -->
    <StreamGeometry x:Key="PhPauseFill">M0 0ZM24 24ZM7.9 4.5L10 4.5Q11 4.5 11 5.5L11 18.5Q11 19.5 10 19.5L7.9 19.5Q6.9 19.5 6.9 18.5L6.9 5.5Q6.9 4.5 7.9 4.5ZM14.6 4.5L16.7 4.5Q17.7 4.5 17.7 5.5L17.7 18.5Q17.7 19.5 16.7 19.5L14.6 19.5Q13.6 19.5 13.6 18.5L13.6 5.5Q13.6 4.5 14.6 4.5Z</StreamGeometry>
    <!-- forward / next: two solid triangles, nose to base, pointing right (the desktop Forward's meaning), a little lower than play like Apple's forward.fill -->
    <StreamGeometry x:Key="PhForwardFill">M0 0ZM24 24ZM2.63 6.51L10.31 11.01Q12 12 10.31 12.99L2.63 17.49Q0.9 18.5 0.9 16.49L0.9 7.51Q0.9 5.5 2.63 6.51ZM13.73 6.51L21.41 11.01Q23.1 12 21.41 12.99L13.73 17.49Q12 18.5 12 16.49L12 7.51Q12 5.5 13.73 6.51Z</StreamGeometry>
